COIN
A minimal instruction set computer (MISC) design. Implemented in CALM.

SPECS
Ram: 64 KiB
Reg. File: 16 (1 B per reg., r0 tied to 0)
Call Stk.: 16 B (8 addresses)
Data Pntr.: 2 B
Inst. Pntr.: 2 B

ARCHITECTURE NOTES
- Program is stored starting at 0x0, which is also where IP starts.
- DP starts at 0x400.

INSTRUCTIONS
[opc 4] [rx 4] [ry 4] [rz 4]
[opc 4] [rx 4] [data 8]

OPCODES
0: LDI - rx = data
1: SHR - rx = (ry >> rz)
2: CLL - push ip; ip = data + rx
3: RET - pop ip
4: AND - rx = ry & rz
5: NOR - rx = ~(ry | rz)
6: ADD - rx = ry + rz
7: SUB - rx = ry - rz
8: JMP - ip = data + rx
9: OUT - print ascii(ram[dp])
a: SKZ - skip if rx == 0
b: SKC - skip if carry
c: MVI - dp = ryrz + rx
d: STO - ram[dp + rx] = data
e: LOD - rx = ram[dp + ry]
f: HLT - halt clock